features Any anatomy

273
00:11:22,210 --> 00:11:23,850
textbook should have
a basic table with

274
00:11:23,850 --> 00:11:26,050
the terminology of
surface bone anatomy.

275
00:11:28,360 --> 00:11:30,930
In part two of this
lecture, we will go

276
00:11:30,930 --> 00:11:32,830
over some basics about
cartilage and its

277
00:11:32,830 --> 00:11:34,770
distribution in the
body, and we will

278
00:11:34,770 --> 00:11:36,570
cover the different
types of joints, and

279
00:11:36,570 --> 00:11:38,770
more specifically,
talk about synovial

280
00:11:38,770 --> 00:11:40,430
joints and how they
can be classified

281
00:11:40,430 --> 00:11:42,510
according to their
potential movements.

282
00:11:44,180 --> 00:11:45,610
There are three types of

283
00:11:45,610 --> 00:11:46,430
cartilages. cartilages.

284
00:11:46,730 --> 00:11:48,110
These three types
have different

285
00:11:48,110 --> 00:11:50,550
histologies, and this
relates directly to

286
00:11:50,550 --> 00:11:52,170
